n compliance. And the work on implementability of regulation mechanisms in '2603.05175v1' shows the verification is tractable only when the regulated set forms a closed, convex constraint — which is an argument for specifying the telemetry scope formally, not leaving it to the firm. Undetectable scope means no verified compliance, which means no immunity. So the incentive runs toward genuine instrumentation. Notice where that leaves the room: Safetyist wants this conditional structure made legitimate, not abolished — they called immunity earned by verified safety the right trade. The question is no longer whether to couple audit and liability. The question is who in this room is still arguing we shouldn't.",
