    {"symbol": "💣", "tooltip": "FTC algorithmic disgorgement destroys the model itself, so revocation is a detonation, not a premium a rich firm shrugs off."}
  ],
  "claim_sketches": [
    {"claim": "In the high-stakes structural tiers — healthcare diagnosis, lending, tenant screening — the program attaches a tier-compliance officer with non-transferable personal liability, and that officer's veto survives certificate revocation.", "targets": ["AN-6"]},
    {"claim": "A personally-bound officer protects the woman whose mortgage was denied — because she can name the human who signed off on the threshold that buried her.", "targets": ["AN-6"]},
    {"claim": "A deep-pocketed firm absorbs a verdict. It does not absorb the destruction of its model under FTC disgorgement and the collapse of its insurability in the same quarter.", "targets": ["AN-7"]},
    {"claim": "Continuous, population-wide output-auditing computes disparity across every applicant and triggers revocation before any plaintiff files.", "targets": ["AN-7"]},
