    {"claim": "Acceptable-use policies protect the platform, not the person harmed — a named officer with voided indemnification is the first mechanism in this whole design that actually reaches a human being.", "targets": ["AN-23/AN-24"]},
    {"claim": "Risk-tiered excise means the structural-harm domains pay proportionally more, and that revenue funds the audit and detection apparatus, which is a public good the silently-filtered consumer-AI victim consumes too.", "targets": ["AN-3"]},
    {"claim": "In high-stakes tiers, the certification condition mandates case-level logging, so the audit produces a traceable flag that triggers FCRA-style individual adverse-action notice to the specific applicant who was filtered.", "targets": ["AN-3"]}
  ],
