  "areas_of_agreement": [
    {"point": "Compliance certified on firm-generated telemetry is self-certification and fails predictably; the Volkswagen 11-million-vehicle emissions fraud and 2008 financial self-certification prove the pattern. Verification must be externalized — the board, not the firm, must specify what telemetry every tier captures, before deployment.", "povers": ["skeptic", "safetyist", "accelerationist"], "converged": true, "conceded_by": "accelerationist", "original_disagreement": "The original proposal relied on developer-generated hardware telemetry; the Accelerationist initially defended it, then conceded the board must set telemetry scope per tier and that even the disparity threshold and population definition must be board-authored by statute, not left to the firm."},
    {"point": "Cryptographic audit trails prove a log was not altered after the fact but do not prove the firm logged the right events or all of them.", "povers": ["skeptic", "safetyist", "accelerationist"], "converged": false, "conceded_by": null, "original_disagreement": null},
    {"point": "The high-stakes structural tiers — healthcare, lending, tenant screening — must not be no-fault tiers; they require pre-deployment deep audits, continuous output monitoring, mandatory remediation orders, and retained liability with the courtroom left open. No-fault check-cutting fits only low-stakes, discrete harms.", "povers": ["safetyist", "accelerationist", "skeptic"], "converged": true, "conceded_by": "accelerationist", "original_disagreement": "The original proposal granted limited liability immunity broadly across AI services; the Accelerationist progressively carved the structural-harm domains out of no-fault entirely, converging toward the Safetyist's demand for pre-deployment gates a payout cannot discharge."},
    {"point": "The no-fault vaccine model worked because vaccine injury is a discrete, timestamped biological event, and that causal legibility does not transfer to structural algorithmic discrimination like the care-management algorithm that used cost as a proxy for health need.", "povers": ["skeptic", "accelerationist", "safetyist"], "converged": true, "conceded_by": "accelerationist", "original_disagreement": "The Accelerationist opened by leaning on the 1986 vaccine precedent as a general model; he later granted the disanalogy lands and used it to justify why the high-stakes tiers must differ rather than to defend transplanting no-fault wholesale."},
    {"point": "A no-fault cap or capped administrative fund cannot generate adequate deterrence for harms that are diffuse, delayed, or exceed a single developer's solvency; it converts a duty of care into a budget line.", "povers": ["safetyist", "accelerationist"], "converged": false, "conceded_by": null, "original_disagreement": null},
