    {"point": "The fairness threshold the board mandates is a contested political choice, not a technical fact, because Chouldechova's 2017 impossibility result proves you cannot simultaneously equalize false-positive rates and calibrate predictions across groups when base rates differ; the board must pick and publish the criterion per tier.", "povers": ["skeptic", "accelerationist"], "converged": true, "conceded_by": "accelerationist", "original_disagreement": "The Skeptic forced the issue by citing Chouldechova; the Accelerationist conceded it is a political choice and agreed the board must publish the criterion per tier rather than stamp one number as technical fact."},
