    {"point": "SOX §304-style dollar-clawback is backward-looking and re-engineerable; twenty-three years produced no case stopping an ex-ante salary gross-up, so dollar-clawback alone is a shell.", "povers": ["skeptic", "accelerationist"], "converged": true, "conceded_by": "accelerationist", "original_disagreement": "The Accelerationist initially offered a SOX §304-modeled clawback as the indemnification wall; after the Skeptic's gross-up critique, he conceded the dollars leak and shifted to barring the D&O coverage product itself."},
